body:
Closes #615.

## Outcome
Fix the authenticated-dashboard acceptance runner so its default Docker Compose project name is valid without requiring a manual `COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME` override.

## Scope
- generate the default UTC run suffix with lowercase `t`/`z` separators while retaining PID uniqueness;
- preserve explicit caller-provided `COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME` unchanged;
- add dependency-free CI regression coverage that executes the real runner bootstrap and verifies Compose-compatible generated names, independent-run uniqueness and override preservation;
- update State Model v2 to make #615 the sole active Work Package and advance the accepted product baseline to merged #590.

## Safety / boundaries
- acceptance tooling only;
- no application/runtime Compose-name changes;
- no dependency or lockfile changes;
- no dashboard acceptance coverage changes;
- no Modbus or hardware writes;
- no production/site cutover;
- no mandatory cloud/runtime dependency.

## Verification target
Require exact-head Core CI (including the new `test_ci_*.py`), Authenticated Dashboard Acceptance without a manual project-name override, every path-triggered workflow and `NEXOLAB Merge Gate` GREEN before merge. Remote Raspberry Pi/local Windows verification remains unavailable because the Remote Desktop connector is offline and is not required for this repository-only tooling fix.
